\p \v 4 \w And the sons|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Javan|strong="H03120"\w*:
\p \w Elishah|strong="H00473"\w*, \w Tarshish|strong="H08659"\w*, \w the Kittites|strong="H03794"\w*, \w and the Rodanites|strong="H01721"\w*.\f + \fr 10:4 \ft SP and some MT manuscripts (see also LXX and 1 Chronicles 1:7); most MT manuscripts \fqa Dodanites\f* \v 5 \w From these|strong="H00428"\w*, \w the maritime|strong="H00339"\w* \w peoples|strong="H01471"\w* \w separated|strong="H06504"\w* \w into their territories|strong="H00776"\w*, \w vvv|strong="H00376"\w* \w according to their languages|strong="H03956"\w*, \w by clans|strong="H04940"\w* \w within their nations|strong="H01471"\w*.
