\p \v 13 \w So [Hagar] gave|strong="H07121"\w* \w this name|strong="H08034"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w who had spoken|strong="H01696"\w* \w to her|strong="H00413"\w*: “\w You are|strong="H00859"\w* \w the God|strong="H00410"\w* \w who sees me|strong="H07210"\w*,\f + \fr 16:13 \ft Hebrew \fqa El-Roi\f*” \w for|strong="H03588"\w* \w she said|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w Here|strong="H01988"\w* \w I have|strong="H01571"\w* \w seen|strong="H07200"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00310"\w* \w the One who sees me|strong="H07200"\w*!” \v 14 \w Therefore|strong="H05921"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03651"\w* \w the well|strong="H00875"\w* \w was called|strong="H07121"\w* \w vvv|strong="H00883"\w* \w vvv|strong="H00883"\w* \w Beer-lahai-roi|strong="H00883"\w*.\f + \fr 16:14 \fqa Beer-lahai-roi \ft means \fqa well of the Living One who sees me\ft .\f* \w It is located|strong="H02009"\w* \w between|strong="H00996"\w* \w Kadesh|strong="H06946"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00996"\w* \w and Bered|strong="H01260"\w*.
