\p \v 10 \w Now Ephron|strong="H06085"\w* \w was sitting|strong="H03427"\w* \w among|strong="H08432"\w* \w the sons|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Heth|strong="H02845"\w*. \w So in the presence|strong="H00241"\w* \w of all|strong="H03605"\w* \w the Hittites|strong="H01121"\w* \w . . .|strong="H02845"\w* \w who had come|strong="H00935"\w* \w to the gate|strong="H08179"\w* \w of his city|strong="H05892"\w*, \w . . .|strong="H00559"\w* \w Ephron|strong="H06085"\w* \w the Hittite|strong="H02850"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w answered|strong="H06030"\w* \w Abraham|strong="H00085"\w*, \v 11 “\w No|strong="H03808"\w*, \w my lord|strong="H00113"\w*. \w Listen to me|strong="H08085"\w*. \w I give|strong="H05414"\w* you \w the field|strong="H07704"\w*, \w and I give|strong="H05414"\w* \w you the cave|strong="H04631"\w* \w that is in it|strong="H00834"\w*. - \w I give it|strong="H05414"\w* to you \w in the presence|strong="H05869"\w* \w of my people|strong="H01121"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05971"\w*. \w Bury|strong="H06912"\w* \w your dead|strong="H04191"\w*.”
