\p \v 24 \w When her time|strong="H03117"\w* \w came|strong="H04390"\w* \w to give birth|strong="H03205"\w*, \w there were indeed|strong="H02009"\w* \w twins|strong="H08380"\w* \w in her womb|strong="H00990"\w*. \v 25 \w The first|strong="H07223"\w* \w one came out|strong="H03318"\w* \w red|strong="H00132"\w*, \w . . .|strong="H03605"\w* \w covered with hair|strong="H08181"\w* \w like a fur coat|strong="H00155"\w*; \w so they named him|strong="H07121"\w* \w . . .|strong="H08034"\w* \w Esau|strong="H06215"\w*.\f + \fr 25:25 \fqa Esau \ft sounds like a Hebrew term that means \fqa hairy\ft .\f* \v 26 \w After|strong="H00310"\w* \w this|strong="H03651"\w*, \w his brother|strong="H00251"\w* \w came out|strong="H03318"\w* \w grasping|strong="H00270"\w* \w Esau’s|strong="H06215"\w* \w heel|strong="H06119"\w* \w -|strong="H03027"\w*; \w so he was named|strong="H07121"\w* \w . . .|strong="H08034"\w* \w Jacob|strong="H03290"\w*.\f + \fr 25:26 \fqa Jacob \ft means \fqa he grasps the heel \ft or \fqa he deceives\ft .\f* \w And Isaac|strong="H03327"\w* \w was sixty|strong="H08346"\w* \w years old|strong="H01121"\w* \w . . .|strong="H08141"\w* \w when [the twins] were born|strong="H03205"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w*.
