\s1 Judah Pleads for Benjamin
\p \v 18 \w Then Judah|strong="H03063"\w* \w approached|strong="H05066"\w* \w [Joseph]|strong="H00413"\w* \w and said|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w Sir|strong="H00994"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00113"\w*, \w please|strong="H04994"\w* \w let your servant|strong="H05650"\w* \w . . .|strong="H01697"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00241"\w* \w speak|strong="H01696"\w* \w personally to my lord|strong="H00113"\w*. \w Do not|strong="H00408"\w* \w be angry|strong="H02734"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00639"\w* \w with your servant|strong="H05650"\w*, \w for|strong="H03588"\w* \w you are equal to|strong="H03644"\w* \w Pharaoh himself|strong="H06547"\w*. \v 19 \w My lord|strong="H00113"\w* \w asked|strong="H07592"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w his servants|strong="H05650"\w*, \w . . .|strong="H00559"\w* ‘\w Do you have|strong="H03426"\w* . . . \w a father|strong="H00001"\w* \w or|strong="H00176"\w* \w a brother|strong="H00251"\w*?’
\p \v 20 \w And we answered|strong="H00559"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00413"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00113"\w*, ‘\w We have|strong="H03426"\w* . . . \w an elderly|strong="H02205"\w* \w father|strong="H00001"\w* \w and a younger brother|strong="H06996"\w*, \w the child|strong="H03206"\w* \w of his old age|strong="H02208"\w*. \w The boy’s brother|strong="H00251"\w* \w is dead|strong="H04191"\w*. \w He|strong="H01931"\w* \w is the only|strong="H00905"\w* \w one of his mother’s|strong="H00517"\w* \w sons left|strong="H03498"\w*, \w and his father|strong="H00001"\w* \w loves him|strong="H00157"\w*.’
