\p \v 21 \w So the sons|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w* \w did|strong="H06213"\w* \w [as they were told]|strong="H03651"\w*. \w Joseph|strong="H03130"\w* \w gave|strong="H05414"\w* them \w wagons|strong="H05699"\w* \w as|strong="H05921"\w* \w Pharaoh|strong="H06547"\w* \w had instructed|strong="H06310"\w*, \w and he also gave|strong="H05414"\w* them \w provisions|strong="H06720"\w* \w for their journey|strong="H01870"\w*. \v 22 \w -|strong="H03605"\w* \w He gave|strong="H05414"\w* \w new|strong="H02487"\w* \w garments|strong="H08071"\w* \w to each of them|strong="H00376"\w*, \w but to Benjamin|strong="H01144"\w* \w he gave|strong="H05414"\w* \w three|strong="H07969"\w* \w hundred [shekels]|strong="H03967"\w* \w of silver|strong="H03701"\w*\f + \fr 45:22 \fqa 300 shekels \ft is approximately 7.5 pounds or 3.4 kilograms of silver.\f* \w and five|strong="H02568"\w* \w sets|strong="H02487"\w* \w of clothes|strong="H08071"\w*. \v 23 \w And he sent|strong="H07971"\w* \w to his father|strong="H00001"\w* \w the following|strong="H02063"\w*: \w ten|strong="H06235"\w* \w donkeys|strong="H02543"\w* \w loaded|strong="H05375"\w* \w with the best|strong="H02898"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H04714"\w*, \w and ten|strong="H06235"\w* \w female donkeys|strong="H00860"\w* \w loaded|strong="H05375"\w* \w with grain|strong="H01250"\w* \w and bread|strong="H03899"\w* \w and provisions|strong="H04202"\w* \w for his father’s|strong="H00001"\w* \w journey|strong="H01870"\w*.
