\s1 Joseph Comforts His Brothers
\p \v 15 \w When Joseph’s|strong="H03130"\w* \w brothers|strong="H00251"\w* \w saw|strong="H07200"\w* \w that|strong="H03588"\w* \w their father|strong="H00001"\w* \w was dead|strong="H04191"\w*, \w they said|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w What if|strong="H03863"\w* \w Joseph|strong="H03130"\w* \w bears a grudge|strong="H07852"\w*? \w Then he will surely repay|strong="H07725"\w* \w . . .|strong="H07725"\w* us \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w for all|strong="H03605"\w* \w the evil|strong="H07451"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w we did|strong="H01580"\w* \w to him|strong="H00853"\w*.”
\p \v 16 \w So they sent word|strong="H06680"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Joseph|strong="H03130"\w*, \w saying|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w Before|strong="H06440"\w* \w he died|strong="H04194"\w*, \w . . .|strong="H00559"\w* \w your father|strong="H00001"\w* \w commanded|strong="H06680"\w*, \v 17 ‘\w This is what|strong="H03541"\w* \w you are to say|strong="H00559"\w* \w to Joseph|strong="H03130"\w*: \w I beg you|strong="H00577"\w*, \w please|strong="H04994"\w* \w forgive|strong="H05375"\w* \w the transgression|strong="H06588"\w* \w and sin|strong="H02403"\w* \w of your brothers|strong="H00251"\w*, \w for|strong="H03588"\w* \w they did|strong="H01580"\w* \w you wrong|strong="H07451"\w*.’ \w So now, [Joseph]|strong="H06258"\w*, \w please|strong="H04994"\w* \w forgive|strong="H05375"\w* \w the transgression|strong="H06588"\w* \w of the servants|strong="H05650"\w* \w of the God|strong="H00430"\w* \w of your father|strong="H00001"\w*.”
